    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d461">

                <pb facs="0634" n="560" xml:id="pg560"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 841.51/75</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-08-02T15:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 2, 1917, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 5.04 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6877. Mr. Balfour has gone over with me the telegram he sent July 30 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">August 2?</hi>] to Spring Rice for McAdoo about
                    exchange. He represents the position as most perilous. He hopes that the
                    President has seen it and will cause a reply to be sent at earliest possible
                    time.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Page</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
